# Third-party baseline repos (ReflexGrad, ADaPT, etc.), cloned fresh with
# git clone rather than vendored — each has its own nested .git. Any patches
# we make on top are documented in commit messages / handoff notes, not
# tracked here.
#
# external/mpo_reflact/ is the one exception: fetch_and_verify.py and
# SOURCE.md are small, hand-written, and are themselves what makes the
# five actual upstream files (downloaded from a pinned MPO commit, verified
# by SHA-256 in fetch_and_verify.py) reproducible without vendoring MPO's
# code into this repo's own git history -- see SOURCE.md. The downloaded
# files stay ignored; only the two files that make them reproducible are
# tracked.
external/*
!external/mpo_reflact/
external/mpo_reflact/*
!external/mpo_reflact/fetch_and_verify.py
!external/mpo_reflact/SOURCE.md

# ADaPT and Reflexion are plain `git clone`s with their own nested .git, so
# git cannot track files *inside* them without turning them into gitlinks.
# Their provenance files therefore live outside the clones, in
# external/_provenance/, which is tracked normally.
!external/_provenance/

# patch/merge artifacts
*.orig
*.rej
